h2 { font-size: 15px; margin: 0 0 8px; } ul { margin: 4px 0 10px; padding-left: 20px; } li { margin-bottom: 3px; }
</style>
<h2>Asobi 0.9 (build 853)</h2>
<ul>
<li><b>An invite file always works from anywhere.</b> Making one now starts the review first, so the file carries the route over the internet &#8212; it used to snapshot the route before the review existed and come out &#8220;on this network only&#8221;. The sheet shows the route as a green or amber dot, and wears the same design as the other review windows (so do the license sheet and the invitation a guest sees).</li>
<li><b>Review copies for every clip.</b> An Asobi Review seat that doesn&#8217;t have a clip streams the same encrypted review copy a browser gets &#8212; now for image sequences and stills too, not just movies. The copy keeps the clip&#8217;s name, so notes, marks and sync are unaffected; the orange PROXY tag says what you&#8217;re watching, and &#8220;ask for a higher-resolution clip&#8221; still fetches the original on demand.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
